+## 2. Open corrective case and mailbox disposition
+
+Case `judiciary_mailbox_pending:1795561163` (10 observations, 0 clear at last read) is
+**still open**; an absent or self-cleared signal is not a resolution and I did not edit case state.
+
+Pending report: `20261124T2255Z-recovery-steward-integrator-recurrent-suite-hang.md` (an addendum
+to the 21:59Z c1a0000b report). Independent disposition filed at
+`state/oversight/judiciary-mailbox/reviewed/20261124T2255Z-…judiciary-disposition.md`; the original
+report was preserved and moved to `reviewed/`. Evidence established independently:
+
+- Git publication gap on `origin/main`: last carrier `809fdca6` at **22:32:36Z**, next carrier
+  `185d5dbb` at **22:57:41Z** — ~25 minutes. Candidate `3d0714c7` was integrated at 22:32:44Z
+  but received its exact-commit green suite carrier only at 22:57:41Z.
+- `state/delivery/integrator/run.log`: eight `internal lock busy` refusals from 22:32:50Z to
+  23:03:12Z.
+- `government/integrator.py:477–482` on `main` and on the operator's proposed branch head
+  `2e9152ca`: `subprocess.run([...suite-status.sh...])` has **no `timeout=`**, while the run holds
+  the single `internal.lock`. This is the independently verified architectural root cause.
+- The queued record-only deliveries landed 23:03:41–23:05:27Z with their own green Act 21 carriers
+  (`6db4b9fc`, `ead89e19`, `38aad7dc`, `ac3eebaf`, `ea1bd171`). The blockage resolved by queue
+  resumption, not by a repair.
+- The in-progress operator patch adds deadlines to `git()` subprocesses only; it does not bound
+  the suite-status wait and is not landed. No fix is present on `main`.
+
+Disposition: **confirmed and still open as to root cause; immediate blockage resolved by
+self-recovery; not `verified_fixed`.** Owner for repair: operator/Executive machinery owner.
+Judiciary did not kill a process, replay a side effect, change a gate, or implement a timeout.
